# Docker build context exclusions for `@usetheo/memory` standalone image.
# Keeps the context small + prevents leaks of secrets, reviews, audit
# trails, and irrelevant assets into the builder stage.

# Build outputs (the image regenerates dist/ in the builder stage)
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies — the builder runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` from pnpm-lock.yaml
node_modules/

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Environment + secrets (NEVER ship into images)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Project meta / planning / audit trails (massive; not runtime artifacts)
.claude/
docs/
examples/
benchmarks/
plans/
spec/

# Tests (production image excludes tests by design)
tests/
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.test.js
**/*.test-d.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
vitest.config.ts
vitest.*.config.ts

# Docker meta itself
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml

# Top-level docs (CHANGELOG kept out; surfaces via package registry)
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE
README.md

# Lock files for ecosystems we don't build with (pnpm-lock.yaml IS needed —
# the builder runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`)
yarn.lock

# Migration-tooling configs not needed in runtime
drizzle.config.ts

# NOTE: scripts/ is NOT excluded — `pnpm build` runs
# scripts/rewrite-dist-aliases.mjs (postbuild:rewrite-aliases). Excluding it
# breaks the image build.
